title: The Liberals call a vote of no confidence against our Government!
subtitle: We've annoyed them too much...
new-page: true
on-arrival: tried_supporting_kpd = 0
view-if: labour_in_government = 1 and coalition_dissent >= 3 and labour_r < 50
tags: event
go-to: vonc_menu

# Options: spend relations to reduce coalition_dissent, ask for kpd to abstain
# (lmao KPD toleration arc...)

= Vote of No Confidence

The Liberals have called a vote of no confidence against us, as a result of some of our policy actions. If this succeeds, there will be an election in a few months.

@vonc_menu

- @try_assuage: Try to win them back.
- @support_kpd: Could the cpgb save us?
- @let_it_happen: Let the vote happen.

@try_assuage

How do we assuage them.

- @austerity: Enact a massive austerity plan.
- @resources: Maybe grant them a peerage...
- @support_kpd: Could we get the KPD to abstain?
- @let_it_happen: Never mind. Let the vote happen.

@austerity
view-if: welfare >= 0 and not secularized
on-arrival: coalition_dissent = 0; workers_labour -= 10; unemployed_labour -= 10; workers_cpgb += 7; workers_nsdap += 3; unemployed_cpgb += 5; unemployed_nsdap += 5; left_dissent += 15; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 15; reformist_dissent += 5; welfare -= 2; budget += 1; unemployed += 3; cpgb_coalition_dissent += 1; cpgb_relation -= 10 if in_popular_front

Fine. We enacted a massive austerity program to cut welfare, in order to maintain the stability of our coalition. The vote has been called off.

@resources
view-if: secularized = 0
choose-if: resources >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: We have made bribe based honours illegal
subtitle: -3 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1;

While not a very socialist thing to do. Granting a liberal a lordship should get them off our back... for now

@support_kpd
choose-if: cpgb_party_leader = "Campbell"
on-arrival: tried_supporting_kpd = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if kpd_relation < 50 : The CPGB are not on good terms with us ?] [? if (in_grand_coalition and kpd_r < liberals_r) or (in_weimar_coalition and kpd_r < liberals_r): The Communists don't have enough votes. ?]

If the Communists keep us in power, then we will owe them a big debt. This could lead to broader cooperation in the future, but they will need concessions...

@let_it_happen
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; labour_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_popular_front = 0; spd_toleration = 0; foreign_minister_party = "DVP"; interior_minister_party = "Z"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; finance_minister_party = "DVP"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; labor_minister = "Stegerwald"; interior_minister = "Wirth"; finance_minister = "Moldenhauer"; economic_minister = "Curtius"; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser"; foreign_minister = "Stresemann"; agriculture_minister = "Dietrich"; reichswehr_minister = "Groener";  coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 3; new_middle_spd -= 2; workers_spd -= 3 if pro_republic < 50; workers_spd -= 4 if pro_republic < 40; old_middle_nsdap += 4 if pro_republic < 50; new_middle_nsdap += 3 if pro_republic < 50
go-to: let_it_happen_hindenburg if president != "Braun"; let_it_happen_braun if president == "Braun"

@let_it_happen_hindenburg
on-arrival: chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; welfare -= 2;

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor Brüning has been appointed as the head of an acting government, consisting solely of the bourgeois parties. He immediately proceeds to cut welfare spending substantially.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@let_it_happen_braun
on-arrival: spd_caretaker = 1

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Prime Minister [+ prime_minister +] remains as the head of a caretaker government, but no longer has the power to enact new policies.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
